# ==============================================================================
# LeakSanitizer (LSan) Suppression Rules & Test Architecture Division
# ==============================================================================
#
# Division of Responsibility between audio_engine_test.cpp and lsan.supp:
#
# 1. audio_engine_test.cpp (Lyra Application & Subsystem Verification):
#    - Responsible for verifying all Lyra memory management, thread-safety,
#      and context lifecycle correctness.
#    - Test 31 validates active hardware device tracking (g_active_device_count),
#      preventing context destruction while devices are playing.
#    - Test 31 validates safe on-demand re-initialization and 8-thread concurrent
#      enumeration stress without data races.
#    - Test 31 and main() invoke shutdown_local_audio_context() to ensure Lyra
#      explicitly releases all application-allocated audio subsystem resources.
#    - Under ASan/LSan, zero bytes may leak from any Lyra code or miniaudio device/
#      context state.
#
# 2. lsan.supp (External Host OS Audio Daemon Singleton Filter):
#    - When miniaudio selects the JACK backend on Linux (connecting to PipeWire-JACK),
#      the client shared libraries (libjack.so -> libpipewire-0.3.so) initialize
#      process-wide daemon singletons (pw_context, D-Bus connection, RTKit worker,
#      and module loaders) upon jack_client_open().
#    - By design, PipeWire keeps these singletons resident until the process exits.
#    - In addition, Lyra intentionally suppresses dlclose() on Linux audio backends
#      to prevent SIGSEGV crashes caused by PipeWire daemon background threads
#      waking up after memory is unmapped.
#    - These system-level singletons do NOT represent leaks in Lyra's audio engine.
#    - This suppression file instructs LeakSanitizer to ignore allocations originated
#      inside PipeWire and JACK client shared objects, allowing LSan to strictly
#      detect and fail on any real leaks originating from Lyra.
# ==============================================================================

leak:libpipewire
leak:libjack
leak:pw_
leak:jack_
